          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "जकात (jakāt) is a loan from Arabic zakāt, \"alms, a tax on wealth\", which reached Marathi through Persian. Its Arabic root is z-k-w (Lane). Marathi writes the z as ज."
            }
          ]
        },
